wh40k-class-specialization-assassin-shadow-name = Veil of Night
wh40k-class-specialization-assassin-shadow-description = Stealth, NPC distraction, observation, and withdrawal.

wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-01-name = Covenant of Silence
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-01-description = Unlocks the Veil of Night stance. Effects require empty hands or light equipment and end on an overt attack.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-02-name = Soft Footfall
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-02-description = Makes footsteps and actions less noticeable while moving slowly, but running remains noisy.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-03-name = Thermal Trace
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-03-description = Reduces detection by suitable thermal systems without defeating direct sight, cameras, or handheld scanners.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-04-name = Motionless Silhouette
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-04-description = Brief stillness accelerates concealment through the standard stealth component; fast movement resets it.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-05-name = Melt into Shadow
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-05-description = Briefly enables controlled camouflage. Attacking, using a large item, running, or taking heavy damage immediately breaks it.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-06-name = Corner Memory
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-06-description = After losing direct sight, only the Assassin briefly sees a selected target's last known point. This is not detection through walls.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-07-name = Quiet Pocket
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-07-description = Interacting with a small suitable item makes less noise; airlocks, gunfire, and heavy objects are excluded.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-08-name = Prey Mark
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-08-description = Marks one visible target for the Assassin, showing direction and a timer while the observation remains recent.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-09-name = False Trail
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-09-description = Throws a real consumable noise marker that briefly distracts hostile NPCs. It cannot control players or pass through walls.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-10-name = Blind Corner
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-10-description = Breaking direct sight with a marked target clears its attention faster. Requires server-side NPC attention integration.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-11-name = Smoke Veil
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-11-description = Activates a held smoke or concealment grenade with a faster DoAfter; no grenade or smoke is granted for free.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-12-name = Stranger's Silhouette
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-12-description = Briefly places a false audiovisual NPC target at a visible point. Players can recognize the tactical decoy; it is neither a clone nor an impersonation.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-13-name = Sense Danger
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-13-description = Warns when a visible hostile NPC starts searching after recent detection; it reveals neither players nor invisible targets.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-14-name = Shadow Among Shadows
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-14-description = Slow movement in darkness or smoke adds less visibility, but light, fire, and fast running still reveal the Assassin.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-15-name = Afterglow of Vanishing
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-15-description = Breaking sight leaves a brief false noise trail and starts lowering visibility. It fails during face-to-face combat.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-16-name = Silent Passage
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-16-description = Reduces the chance that a distracted or suppressed NPC instantly notices the Assassin nearby. Collision remains fully active.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-17-name = Deep Vanishing
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-17-description = Briefly strengthens camouflage while completely forbidding attacks, item use, and fast movement.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-18-name = Master of Distraction
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-18-description = False Trail and Stranger's Silhouette last longer when the Assassin personally broke direct sight.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-19-name = Unseen Route
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-19-description = After three consecutive sight breaks, temporarily caps visibility during slow movement; attacking or running resets the sequence.
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-20-name = Ghost of the Hive
wh40k-class-skill-assassin-shadow-20-description = Final node: combines camouflage, sight breaks, and distraction in one capped modifier. It grants no permanent invisibility, universal sensor immunity, or camouflage stacking.

ent-ActionWh40kAssassinDissolve = Melt into shadow
    .desc = Enter temporary camouflage. Movement, damage, attacks, or changing the held item break it.
ent-ActionWh40kAssassinPreyMark = Prey mark
    .desc = Mark one visible hostile target for Assassin combinations.
ent-ActionWh40kAssassinFalseTrail = False trail
    .desc = Throw the real distraction item in your active hand and redirect nearby hostile NPCs.
ent-ActionWh40kAssassinSmokeVeil = Smoke veil
    .desc = Throw the real held concealment item and distract nearby hostile NPCs.
ent-ActionWh40kAssassinFalseSilhouette = Stranger's silhouette
    .desc = Throw the real held distraction item to create a short-lived false point of attention for NPCs.
ent-ActionWh40kAssassinVanishingGlimmer = Afterglow of vanishing
    .desc = Leave a strong temporary NPC distraction by throwing the real item in your active hand.
ent-ActionWh40kAssassinDeepVanish = Deep vanishing
    .desc = Enter stronger short-lived camouflage that breaks on movement, damage, attacks, or item changes.
